#question(title: [Taylor polynomial of a polynomial])[
  Let $f(x) = x^3$.

  Let $Q_(n, a)$ be the $n$-th Taylor
  polynomial for $f$ at $a$.
  #v(0.2cm)

  + Using the 2nd definition, find
    $Q_(2, 0)$.

     Then verify it also satisfies the 1st
     definition.
     #v(0.2cm)
  + Repeat for $Q_(3, 0)$
     #v(0.2cm)
  + Repeat for $Q_(3, 1)$
     #v(0.2cm)
  + Repeat for $Q_(2, 1)$.
]
